<diagram id="p0" name="0 Start here"><mxGraphModel dx="1200" dy="800" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1400" pageHeight="600" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="t0" value="ZET database — how to read this (start here)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=22;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#111;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="720" height="36" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="how" value="&lt;b&gt;How to read&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;1. Each colored box is a &lt;b&gt;table&lt;/b&gt; (like a spreadsheet).&lt;br/&gt;2. An arrow means: &lt;b&gt;this column joins that table&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;br/&gt;3. &lt;font color='#b35900'&gt;&lt;b&gt;[PK]&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; = Primary Key (the unique ID of a row).&lt;br/&gt;4. &lt;font color='#b35900'&gt;&lt;b&gt;[FK]&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; = Foreign Key (the join column).&lt;br/&gt;5. Blue text like &lt;font color='#1565c0'&gt;→ users.id&lt;/font&gt; shows exactly what it joins.&lt;br/&gt;6. Use the &lt;b&gt;tabs at the bottom&lt;/b&gt; — each page is one simple topic so lines stay clear." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fillColor=#fffde7;strokeColor=#f9a825;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="70" width="560" height="180" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="s_users" value="users
